1
00:00:01,569 --> 00:00:09,729
Chapter 18 Merry days were these at Thornfield Hall, and busy days, too.

2
00:00:10,049 --> 00:00:13,523
How different from the first three months of stillness,

3
00:00:13,524 --> 00:00:16,830
monotony, and solitude I had passed beneath its roof.

4
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:23,690
All sad feelings seemed now driven from the house, or gloomy associations forgotten.

5
00:00:24,259 --> 00:00:28,330
There was life everywhere, movement all day long.

6
00:00:29,229 --> 00:00:34,330
You could not now traverse the gallery, once so hushed, nor enter the front

7
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:36,918
chambers, once so tenantless, without

8
00:00:36,919 --> 00:00:40,591
encountering a smart lady's made or a dandy valet.

9
00:00:41,189 --> 00:00:46,330
The kitchen, the butler's pantry, the servants hall, the entrance hall,

10
00:00:46,889 --> 00:00:53,450
were equally alive, and the saloons were only left void and still, when the blue

11
00:00:53,451 --> 00:00:56,808
sky and halcyon sunshine of the genial spring

12
00:00:56,858 --> 00:01:00,240
weather called their occupants out into the grounds.

13
00:01:01,470 --> 00:01:06,349
Even when that weather was broken, and continuous rain set in for some days,

14
00:01:07,169 --> 00:01:09,290
no damp seemed cast over enjoyment.

15
00:01:10,369 --> 00:01:15,930
Indoor amusements only became more lively and varied in consequence of the stop put

16
00:01:16,479 --> 00:01:17,669
