It was not elicited by meritricious arts and calculated maneuvers, and one had but

230
00:18:40,250 --> 00:18:46,290
to accept it, to answer what he asked without pretension, to address him when

231
00:18:46,290 --> 00:18:51,550
needful without grimace, and it increased and grew kinder and more genial,

232
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:55,110
and warmed one like a fostering sunbeam.

233
00:18:56,059 --> 00:18:58,870
How will she manage to please him when they are married?

234
00:18:59,849 --> 00:19:05,309
I do not think she will manage it, and yet it might be managed, and his wife

235
00:19:05,311 --> 00:19:11,830
might, I verily believe, be the very happiest woman, the sun shines on.

236
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:17,601
I have not yet said anything condemnatory of Mr. Rochester's

237
00:19:17,603 --> 00:19:20,230
project of marrying for interest and connections.

238
00:19:21,970 --> 00:19:26,190
It surprised me when I first discovered that such was his intention.

239
00:19:27,889 --> 00:19:33,250
I had thought him a man unlikely to be influenced by motives so commonplace in

240
00:19:33,250 --> 00:19:39,250
his choice of a wife, but the longer I considered the position, education, etc.

241
00:19:39,650 --> 00:19:44,930
, of the parties, the less I felt justified in judging and blaming,

242
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:50,230
either him or Miss Ingram for acting in conformity to ideas and principles

243
00:19:50,629 --> 00:19:54,050
instilled into them, doubtless from their childhood.

244
00:19:55,220 --> 00:19:57,430
All their class held these principles.

245
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:03,629
I suppose then they had reasons for holding them such as I could not fathom.

246
00:20:04,669 --> 00:20:10,389
It seemed to me that, where I a gentleman like him, I would take to my bosom only

247
00:20:10,391 --> 00:20:16,129
such a wife as I could love, but the very obviousness of the advantages to the

248
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:22,449
husband's own happiness offered by this plan convinced me that there must be

249
00:20:22,451 --> 00:20:29,849
arguments against its general adoption of which I was quite ignorant, otherwise I

250
00:20:29,851 --> 00:20:33,389
felt sure all the world would act as I wished to act.

251
00:20:34,449 --> 00:20:39,550
But in other points, as well as this, I was growing very lenient to my master.

252
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:44,889
I was forgetting all his faults, for which I had once kept a sharp lookout.

253
00:20:44,891 --> 00:20:51,569
It had formerly been my endeavour to study all sides of his character, to take the

254
00:20:51,571 --> 00:20:58,050
bad with the good, and from the just weighing of both, to form an equitable judgment.

255
00:20:58,430 --> 00:21:00,150
Now I saw no bad.

256
00:21:01,334 --> 00:21:05,989
The sarcasm that had repelled, the harshness that had startled me once,

257
00:21:06,569 --> 00:21:09,330
were only like keen condiments in a choice dish.

258
00:21:10,230 --> 00:21:15,870
Their presence was pungent, but their absence would be felt as comparatively

259
00:21:16,345 --> 00:21:22,489
insipid, and as for the vague something, was it a sinister or a sorrowful,

260
00:21:23,069 --> 00:21:25,650
a designing or a desponding expression?

261
00:21:27,029 --> 00:21:33,250
That opened upon a careful observer, now and then, in his eye, and closed again

262
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:37,629
before one could fathom the strange depth partially disclosed.

263
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:43,910
That's something which used to make me fear and shrink, as if I had been

264
00:21:43,911 --> 00:21:48,730
wandering amongst volcanic-looking hills, and had suddenly felt the ground quiver

265
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:50,180
and seen it gap.

266
00:21:50,949 --> 00:21:56,750
That's something I, at intervals, beheld still, and with throbbing heart,

267
00:21:57,250 --> 00:21:58,430
but not with palsyed nerves.

268
00:21:59,449 --> 00:22:06,050
Instead of wishing to shun, I longed only to dare, to divine it, and I thought Miss

269
00:22:06,050 --> 00:22:10,790
Ingram happy, because one day she might look into the abyss at her leisure,

270
00:22:11,389 --> 00:22:14,930
explore its secrets, and analyse their nature.

271
00:22:16,069 --> 00:22:21,370
Meantime, while I thought only of my master and his future bride, saw only

272
00:22:21,370 --> 00:22:26,269
them, heard only their discourse, and considered only their movements of

273
00:22:26,271 --> 00:22:29,599
importance, the rest of the party were occupied

274
00:22:29,599 --> 00:22:33,150
with their own separate interests and pleasures.

275
00:22:35,410 --> 00:22:40,169
The ladies Lin and Ingram continued to consort in solemn conferences,

276
00:22:41,105 --> 00:22:46,790
where they nodded their two turbans at each other, and held up their forehands in

277
00:22:46,790 --> 00:22:52,730
confronting gestures of surprise or mystery or horror, according to the theme

278
00:22:52,730 --> 00:22:59,489
on which their gossip ran, like a pair of magnified puppets, mild Mrs. Dent talked

279
00:22:59,491 --> 00:23:02,131
with good-natured Mrs. Eshton, and the two

280
00:23:02,133 --> 00:23:05,370
sometimes bestowed a courteous word or smile on me.

281
00:23:08,010 --> 00:23:12,122
So George Lin, Colonel Dent, and Mr. Eshton discussed

282
00:23:12,124 --> 00:23:15,949
politics, or county affairs, or justice business.

283
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:22,910
Lord Ingram flirted with Amy Eshton, Luisa played and sang two and with one of

284
00:23:22,911 --> 00:23:25,599
the messes Lin, and Mary Ingram listened

285
00:23:25,599 --> 00:23:29,750
languidly to the gallant speeches of the other.

286
00:23:30,059 --> 00:23:34,214
Sometimes all, as with one consent, suspended their

287
00:23:34,216 --> 00:23:37,110
bi-play to observe and listen to the principal actors.

288
00:23:37,970 --> 00:23:43,650
Four, after all, Mr. Rochester and, because closely connected with him,

289
00:23:44,430 --> 00:23:47,190
Miss Ingram were the life and soul of the party.

290
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:53,129
If he was absent from the room an hour, a perceptible dullness seemed to steal

291
00:23:53,131 --> 00:23:57,750
over the spirits of his guests, and his re-entrance was sure to give a

292
00:23:57,750 --> 00:24:00,669
fresh impulse to the vivacity of conversation.

293
00:24:02,250 --> 00:24:07,870
The want of his animating influence appeared to be peculiarly felt one day

294
00:24:08,370 --> 00:24:10,841
that he had been summoned to Mill Court on

295
00:24:10,843 --> 00:24:14,351
business, and was not likely to return till late.

296
00:24:15,849 --> 00:24:17,089
The afternoon was wet.

297
00:24:17,989 --> 00:24:22,910
A walk the party had proposed to take to see a gypsy camp, lately pitched on a

298
00:24:22,911 --> 00:24:26,330
common beyond hay, was consequently deferred.

299
00:24:27,389 --> 00:24:29,750
Some of the gentlemen were gone to the stables.

300
00:24:30,669 --> 00:24:33,885
The younger ones, together with the younger ladies,

301
00:24:33,887 --> 00:24:36,430
were playing billiards in the billiard room.

302
00:24:37,269 --> 00:24:41,730
The Dowagers, Ingram and Lin sought solace in a quiet game at cards.

303
00:24:42,775 --> 00:24:49,750
Blanch Ingram, after having repelled by super-cilious taciturnity, some efforts of

304
00:24:49,750 --> 00:24:56,349
Mrs. Dent and Mrs. Eshton to draw her into conversation, had first murmured over some

305
00:24:56,351 --> 00:25:02,150
sentimental tunes and heirs on the piano, and then, having fetched a novel from the

306
00:25:02,150 --> 00:25:07,849
library, had flung herself in haughty listlessness on a sofa, and prepared to

307
00:25:07,851 --> 00:25:12,989
beguile by the spell of fiction, the tedious hours of absence.

308
00:25:14,739 --> 00:25:16,250
The room in the house was silent.

309
00:25:17,389 --> 00:25:22,209
Only now and then, the merriment of the billiard players was heard from above.

310
00:25:23,319 --> 00:25:28,690
It was verging on dusk, and the clock had already given warning of the hour to dress

311
00:25:28,690 --> 00:25:33,250
for dinner, when Little Adele, who knelt by me in the drawing-room window

312
00:25:33,250 --> 00:25:39,690
-seat, suddenly exclaimed, Voila, Monsieur Roche-Stere, Girevion.

313
00:25:41,349 --> 00:25:46,629
I turned, and Miss Ingram darted forwards from her sofa, the others too,

314
00:25:47,169 --> 00:25:52,029
looked up from their several occupations, for at the same time a crunching of wheels

315
00:25:52,031 --> 00:25:56,290
and a splashing tramp of horse hooves became audible on the wet gravel,

316
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:58,410
a post-chase was approaching.

317
00:26:00,309 --> 00:26:03,449
What can possess him to come home in that style?

318
00:26:04,449 --> 00:26:05,449
said Miss Ingram.

319
00:26:06,669 --> 00:26:09,648
He rode Miss Roer, the black horse, did he

320
00:26:09,648 --> 00:26:13,351
not, when he went out, and Pyle was with him.

321
00:26:13,730 --> 00:26:15,091
What has he done with the animals?

322
00:26:17,010 --> 00:26:22,629
As she said this, she approached her tall person and ample garment so near the

323
00:26:22,631 --> 00:26:27,889
window that I was obliged to bend back almost to the breaking of my spine.

324
00:26:29,319 --> 00:26:34,125
In her eagerness she did not observe me at first, but when

325
00:26:34,127 --> 00:26:38,290
she did, she curled her lip and moved to another casement.

326
00:26:39,290 --> 00:26:44,790
The post-chase stopped, the driver rang the doorbell, and a gentleman alighted a

327
00:26:44,790 --> 00:26:48,669
tired in traveling garb, but it was not Mr. Rochester.

328
00:26:49,669 --> 00:26:53,209
It was a tall, fashionable looking man, a stranger.

329
00:26:55,059 --> 00:27:02,010
How provoking, exclaimed Miss Ingram, you tire some monkey, a post-refizing

330
00:27:02,010 --> 00:27:06,230
Adele, who perched you up in the window to give false intelligence.

331
00:27:07,480 --> 00:27:11,510
And she cast on me an angry glance as if I were in fault.

332
00:27:13,319 --> 00:27:17,190
Some parliing was audible in the hall, and soon the newcomer entered.

333
00:27:17,970 --> 00:27:21,889
He bowed to Lady Ingram, as deeming her the eldest lady present.

334
00:27:23,949 --> 00:27:29,830
It appears I come at an inopportune-time madam, said he, when my friend Mr.

335
00:27:30,010 --> 00:27:31,349
Rochester is from home.

336
00:27:32,375 --> 00:27:37,970
But I arrive from a very long journey, and I think I may presume so far on old

337
00:27:37,970 --> 00:27:42,089
and intimate acquaintance, and as to install myself here till he returns.

338
00:27:43,410 --> 00:27:44,449
His manner was polite.

339
00:27:45,319 --> 00:27:49,866
His accent, in speaking, struck me as being somewhat unusual,

340
00:27:49,868 --> 00:27:53,849
not precisely foreign, but still not altogether English.

341
00:27:55,300 --> 00:27:57,790
His age might be about Mr. Rochester's.

342
00:27:58,514 --> 00:28:04,002
Between 30 and 40, his complexion was singularly salo, otherwise

343
00:28:04,004 --> 00:28:07,910
he was a fine -looking man, at first sight, especially.

344
00:28:09,120 --> 00:28:13,849
On closer examination, you detected something in his face that displeased,

345
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:16,169
or rather that failed to please.

346
00:28:17,129 --> 00:28:19,849
His features were regular but too relaxed.

347
00:28:20,730 --> 00:28:24,088
His eye was large and well-cut, but the life looking

348
00:28:24,089 --> 00:28:27,650
out of it was a tame vacant life, at least so I thought.

349
00:28:29,019 --> 00:28:32,118
The sound of the dressing-bell dispersed the party,

350
00:28:32,118 --> 00:28:35,029
it was not till after dinner that I saw him again.

351
00:28:36,069 --> 00:28:42,851
He then seemed quite at his ease, but I liked his physiognomy even less than before.

352
00:28:43,209 --> 00:28:47,830
It struck me as being at the same time unsettled and inanimate.

353
00:28:49,029 --> 00:28:52,730
His eye wandered, and had no meaning in its wandering.

354
00:28:53,430 --> 00:28:57,110
This gave him an odd look, such as I never remembered to have seen.

355
00:28:58,330 --> 00:29:03,209
For a handsome and not an unamiable looking man, he repelled me exceedingly.

356
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:08,589
There was no power in that smooth skinned face of a full oval shape.

357
00:29:09,589 --> 00:29:13,389
No firmness in that aquiline nose and small cherry mouth.

358
00:29:14,394 --> 00:29:21,071
There was no thought on the low even forehead, no command in that blank brown eye.

359
00:29:22,540 --> 00:29:26,345
As I sat in my usual nook and looked at him with the light

360
00:29:26,347 --> 00:29:29,930
of the gerandales on the mantelpiece beaming full over him.

361
00:29:31,029 --> 00:29:34,599
For he occupied an armchair, drawn close to the fire,

362
00:29:34,601 --> 00:29:38,790
and kept shrinking still nearer, as if he was cold.

363
00:29:39,529 --> 00:29:41,410
I compared him with Mr. Rochester.

364
00:29:43,209 --> 00:29:48,989
I think, with deference be it spoken, the contrast could not be much greater

365
00:29:48,991 --> 00:29:53,036
between a leak, gander, and a fierce falcon between a meek

366
00:29:53,038 --> 00:29:56,489
sheep and the rough -coated keen-eyed dog, its guardian.

367
00:29:57,580 --> 00:30:00,830
He had spoken of Mr. Rochester as an old friend.

368
00:30:01,709 --> 00:30:04,069
A curious friendship theirs must have been.

369
00:30:05,110 --> 00:30:11,430
A pointed illustration, indeed, of the old adage that extremes meet.

370
00:30:13,589 --> 00:30:21,589
Two or three of the conversation across the room.

371
00:30:22,660 --> 00:30:26,470
At first I could not make much sense of what I heard.

372
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:32,410
For the discourse of Luisa Eshton and Mary Ingram, who sat near it to me,

373
00:30:33,250 --> 00:30:37,381
confused the fragmentary sentences that reached me at

374
00:30:37,383 --> 00:30:40,269
intervals, these last were discussing the stranger.

375
00:30:41,084 --> 00:30:43,629
They both called him a beautiful man.

376
00:30:44,449 --> 00:30:51,209
Luisa said he was a love of a creature, and she adored him, and Mary instanced his

377
00:30:51,584 --> 00:30:55,510
pretty little mouth and nice nose as her ideal of the charming.

378
00:30:57,050 --> 00:31:00,669
And what a sweet, tempered forehead he has, cried Luisa.

379
00:31:01,349 --> 00:31:05,849
So smooth, none of those frowning irregularities I dislike so much,

380
00:31:06,550 --> 00:31:08,349
and such a placid eye and smile.

381
00:31:09,730 --> 00:31:15,510
And then, to my great relief, Mr. Henry Lin summoned them to the other side of the

382
00:31:15,510 --> 00:31:20,889
room to settle some point about the deferred excursion to hey common.

383
00:31:22,260 --> 00:31:28,209
I was now able to concentrate my attention on the group by the fire, and I presently

384
00:31:28,211 --> 00:31:32,730
gathered that the newcomer was called Mr. Mason.

385
00:31:34,440 --> 00:31:39,470
Then I learned that he was but just arrived in England and that he came from

386
00:31:39,470 --> 00:31:44,849
some hot country, which was the reason, doubtless, his face was so salo,

387
00:31:45,529 --> 00:31:49,529
and that he sat so near the hearth and wore a shirt out in the house.

388
00:31:50,889 --> 00:31:58,889
Presently, the words Jamaica, Kingston, Spanish Town indicated the West Indies as

389
00:31:58,891 --> 00:32:05,150
his residence, and it was with no little surprise I gathered air long, that he had

390
00:32:05,150 --> 00:32:08,269
their first scene and become acquainted with Mr. Rochester.

391
00:32:09,610 --> 00:32:13,470
He spoke of his friends dislike of the burning heats, the hurricanes,

392
00:32:14,569 --> 00:32:16,809
and rainy seasons of that region.

393
00:32:18,230 --> 00:32:25,269
I knew Mr. Rochester had been a traveler, Mrs. Fairfax had said so, but I thought

394
00:32:25,271 --> 00:32:28,269
the continent of Europe had bounded his wanderings.

395
00:32:29,224 --> 00:32:33,650
Till now, I had never heard a hint given a visit to more distant shores.

396
00:32:35,089 --> 00:32:40,290
I was pondering these things, when an incident and a somewhat unexpected one

397
00:32:40,889 --> 00:32:42,610
broke the thread of my musings.

398
00:32:44,930 --> 00:32:50,889
Mr. Mason, shivering as someone chance to open the door, asked for more coal to be

399
00:32:50,891 --> 00:32:53,985
put on the fire, which had burnt out its flame,

400
00:32:53,987 --> 00:32:57,650
though its mass of cinder still shone hot and red.

401
00:32:58,830 --> 00:33:04,730
The footmen who brought the coal in going out, stopped near Mr. Eston's chair and

402
00:33:04,730 --> 00:33:11,910
said something to him in a low voice of which I heard only the words, old woman,

403
00:33:12,910 --> 00:33:14,110
quite troublesome.

404
00:33:15,809 --> 00:33:19,389
Tell her she shall be put in the stocks if she does not take herself off,

405
00:33:19,870 --> 00:33:21,069
replied the magistrate.

406
00:33:22,190 --> 00:33:24,769
No, stop interrupted Colonel Dent.

407
00:33:26,099 --> 00:33:27,650
Don't send her away, Eston.

408
00:33:28,379 --> 00:33:31,669
We might turn the thing to account, better consult the ladies.

409
00:33:32,940 --> 00:33:35,089
And speaking aloud, he continued.

410
00:33:36,529 --> 00:33:41,370
Ladies, you talked of going to hey common to visit the gypsy camp.

411
00:33:42,069 --> 00:33:46,150
Sam here says that one of the old mother -bunches is in the servants' hall at this

412
00:33:46,150 --> 00:33:49,067
moment, and insists upon being brought in

413
00:33:49,069 --> 00:33:52,930
before the quality to tell them their fortunes.

414
00:33:54,010 --> 00:33:55,050
Would you like to see her?

415
00:33:56,129 --> 00:34:01,550
Surely Colonel cried Lady Ingram, you would not encourage such a low

416
00:34:01,550 --> 00:34:04,870
imposter, dismiss her by all means at once.

417
00:34:06,529 --> 00:34:09,612
But I cannot persuade her to go away my lady,

418
00:34:09,614 --> 00:34:13,311
said the footmen, nor can any of the servants.

419
00:34:13,849 --> 00:34:18,430
Mrs. Fairfax is with her just now, in treating her to be gone.

420
00:34:19,440 --> 00:34:24,370
But she has taken a chair in the chimney corner, and says nothing shall stir her

421
00:34:24,370 --> 00:34:27,230
from it till she gets leave to come in here.

422
00:34:28,970 --> 00:34:29,970
What does she want?

423
00:34:30,809 --> 00:34:32,029
asked Mrs. Eston.

424
00:34:33,190 --> 00:34:36,188
To tell the gentry their fortunes, she says,

425
00:34:36,188 --> 00:34:39,370
ma'am, and she swears she must and will do it.

426
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:41,480
What is she like?

427
00:34:42,250 --> 00:34:47,529
inquired the Mrs. Eston in a breath, a shockingly ugly old creature miss,

428
00:34:48,290 --> 00:34:49,989
almost as black as a croc.

429
00:34:51,339 --> 00:34:55,470
Why, she's a real sorceress, cried Frederick Lynn.

430
00:34:56,430 --> 00:34:57,769
Let us have her in, of course.

431
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:02,108
To be sure, rejoined his brother, it would be a

432
00:35:02,108 --> 00:35:04,870
thousand pities to throw away such a chance of fun.

433
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:09,730
My dear boys, what are you thinking about?

434
00:35:10,650 --> 00:35:11,830
Exclaimed Mrs. Lynn.

435
00:35:13,050 --> 00:35:16,230
I cannot possibly countenance any such inconsistent

436
00:35:16,232 --> 00:35:18,830
proceeding, chimed in the Dowager Ingram.

437
00:35:19,750 --> 00:35:25,629
Indeed, ma'am, but you can, and will, pronounce the haughty voice of Blanche,

438
00:35:26,110 --> 00:35:30,089
as she turned round on the piano stool, where till now she had sat silent,

439
00:35:30,769 --> 00:35:33,050
apparently examining sundry sheets of music.

440
00:35:34,879 --> 00:35:41,430
I have a curiosity to hear my fortune told, therefore Sam, order the bell-dame forward.

441
00:35:42,180 --> 00:35:47,349
My darling Blanche, recollect, I do, I recollect all you can suggest,

442
00:35:47,974 --> 00:35:50,010
and I must have my will, quick Sam.

443
00:35:51,220 --> 00:35:56,529
Yes, yes, yes, cried all the juveniles, both ladies and gentlemen, let her come,

444
00:35:57,180 --> 00:35:58,510
it will be excellent sport.

445
00:35:59,459 --> 00:36:00,569
The footman still lingered.

446
00:36:01,610 --> 00:36:04,349
She looked such a rough one, said he.

447
00:36:05,110 --> 00:36:08,870
Go, a jack-ulated Miss Ingram, and the man went.

448
00:36:10,489 --> 00:36:13,881
Excitement instantly seized the whole party, a running

449
00:36:13,881 --> 00:36:16,809
fire of railery and jests was proceeding when Sam returned.

450
00:36:17,489 --> 00:36:19,650
She won't come now, said he.

451
00:36:20,449 --> 00:36:25,169
She says, it's not her mission to appear before the vulgar herd, them's her words.

452
00:36:26,099 --> 00:36:31,589
I must show her into a room by herself, and then those who wish to consult her

453
00:36:32,040 --> 00:36:33,889
must go to her one by one.

454
00:36:35,830 --> 00:36:43,830
You see now my queenly Blanche began lady Ingram, she encroaches, be advised my

455
00:36:43,830 --> 00:36:50,790
angel girl, and show her into the library of course, cut in the angel girl.

456
00:36:52,139 --> 00:36:56,150
It is not my mission to listen to her before the vulgar herd, either.

457
00:36:56,985 --> 00:37:01,190
I mean to have her all to myself, is there a fire in the library?

458
00:37:02,370 --> 00:37:05,629
Yes, ma'am, but she looks such a tinkler.

459
00:37:06,790 --> 00:37:09,250
Seized that chatter blockhead and do my bidding.

460
00:37:10,099 --> 00:37:16,911
Again, Sam vanished, and mystery, animation, expectation rose to full flow once more.

461
00:37:18,379 --> 00:37:20,489
She's ready now, said the footman.

462
00:37:20,940 --> 00:37:24,589
As he reappeared, she wishes to know who will be her first visitor.

463
00:37:25,940 --> 00:37:28,455
I think I had better just look in upon her

464
00:37:28,457 --> 00:37:32,470
before any of the lady's go, said Colonel Dent.

465
00:37:33,440 --> 00:37:36,309
Tell her, Sam, a gentleman is coming.

466
00:37:37,620 --> 00:37:38,769
Sam went and returned.

467
00:37:40,040 --> 00:37:44,449
She says, sir, that she'll have no gentleman, they need not trouble

468
00:37:44,451 --> 00:37:49,510
themselves to come near her, nor he added, with difficulty suppressing a titter.

469
00:37:50,709 --> 00:37:53,730
Any ladies, either, accept the young and single.

470
00:37:55,260 --> 00:37:58,750
By Jov, she has taste, exclaimed Henry Lynn.

471
00:38:00,269 --> 00:38:05,889
Miss Ingram rose solemnly, I go first, she said, in a tone which might have

472
00:38:05,891 --> 00:38:10,410
befitted the leader of a fallon hope, mounting a breach in the van of his men.

473
00:38:11,269 --> 00:38:19,269
Oh, my best, oh, my dearest, pause, reflect, was her mama's cry, but she swept

474
00:38:19,271 --> 00:38:22,891
past her in stately silence, passed through the door which

475
00:38:22,892 --> 00:38:26,930
Colonel Dent held open, and we heard her enter the library.

476
00:38:28,180 --> 00:38:29,970
A comparative silence ensued.

477
00:38:30,910 --> 00:38:36,349
Lady Ingram thought it, La Cass to ring her hands, which she did accordingly.

478
00:38:38,160 --> 00:38:42,970
Miss Mary declared she felt, for her part, she never dared venture.

479
00:38:44,169 --> 00:38:48,330
Amy and Luisa Eston titted under their breath and looked a little frightened.

480
00:38:50,290 --> 00:38:56,949
The minutes passed very slowly, 15 were counted before the library door again opened.

481
00:38:57,970 --> 00:39:00,944
Miss Ingram returned to us through the arch,

482
00:39:00,946 --> 00:39:04,430
would she laugh, would she take it as a joke?

483
00:39:04,980 --> 00:39:09,097
All eyes met her with a glance of eager curiosity, and

484
00:39:09,099 --> 00:39:12,849
she met all eyes with one of her buff and coldness.

485
00:39:13,510 --> 00:39:15,550
She looked neither flurried nor Mary.

486
00:39:16,230 --> 00:39:19,230
She walked stiffly to her seat and took it in silence.

487
00:39:21,040 --> 00:39:23,089
Well-blanch said Lord Ingram.

488
00:39:24,330 --> 00:39:25,650
What did she say, sister?

489
00:39:26,309 --> 00:39:27,309
Asked Mary.

490
00:39:28,050 --> 00:39:29,050
What did you think?

491
00:39:29,529 --> 00:39:30,529
How do you feel?

492
00:39:30,769 --> 00:39:32,349
Is she a real fortune teller?

493
00:39:32,849 --> 00:39:33,989
Demanded the Mrs. Eston.

494
00:39:35,089 --> 00:39:36,269
Now, now, good people.

495
00:39:37,150 --> 00:39:38,150
Returned Miss Ingram.

496
00:39:38,650 --> 00:39:39,650
Don't press upon me.

497
00:39:40,449 --> 00:39:45,230
Really, your organs of wonder and credulity are easily excited.

498
00:39:46,129 --> 00:39:48,970
You seem, by the importance of you all.

499
00:39:49,650 --> 00:39:50,849
My good Mama included.

500
00:39:51,650 --> 00:39:56,470
Ascribed to this matter, absolutely to believe we have a genuine witch in the

501
00:39:56,470 --> 00:39:59,870
house, who is in close alliance with the old gentleman.

502
00:40:01,139 --> 00:40:03,209
I have seen a gypsy vagabond.

503
00:40:03,849 --> 00:40:07,269
She has practised in hackneyed fashion the science of

504
00:40:07,271 --> 00:40:10,470
palmistry and told me what such people usually tell.

505
00:40:11,839 --> 00:40:13,349
My whim is gratified.

506
00:40:14,330 --> 00:40:19,569
And now I think Mr. Eston will do well to put the hag in the stocks tomorrow morning

507
00:40:19,669 --> 00:40:20,669
as he threatened.

508
00:40:22,440 --> 00:40:25,489
Miss Ingram took a book, lent back in her

509
00:40:25,489 --> 00:40:28,730
chair, and so declined further conversation.

510
00:40:29,470 --> 00:40:31,669
I watched her for nearly half an hour.

511
00:40:32,410 --> 00:40:37,650
During all that time she never turned a page, and her face grew momently darker,

512
00:40:38,209 --> 00:40:43,110
more dissatisfied, and more sourly expressive of disappointment.

513
00:40:43,910 --> 00:40:46,750
She had obviously not heard anything to her advantage.

514
00:40:47,870 --> 00:40:53,650
And it seemed to me, from her prolonged fit of gloom and taciturnity, that she

515
00:40:53,650 --> 00:40:58,690
herself, notwithstanding her professed indifference, attached

516
00:40:58,692 --> 00:41:02,309
undue importance to whatever revelations had been made her.

517
00:41:02,870 --> 00:41:09,970
Meantime, Mary Ingram, Amy and Louisa Eston declared they dared not go alone.

518
00:41:10,694 --> 00:41:13,169
And yet they all wished to go.

519
00:41:14,540 --> 00:41:17,730
A negotiation was open through the medium of the ambassador, Sam.

520
00:41:18,540 --> 00:41:22,552
And after much pacing, two-and-fro, till, I think, the

521
00:41:22,553 --> 00:41:25,290
said Sam's calves must have ached with the exercise.

522
00:41:26,260 --> 00:41:31,730
Permission was at last, with great difficulty, extorted from the rigorous

523
00:41:31,730 --> 00:41:35,129
sibil, for the three to wait upon her in a body.

524
00:41:36,419 --> 00:41:40,650
Their visit was not so still as Miss Ingram's had been.

525
00:41:41,629 --> 00:41:46,209
We heard hysterical giggling and little shrieks proceeding from the library,

526
00:41:46,809 --> 00:41:51,709
and at the end of about twenty minutes, they burst the door open and came running

527
00:41:51,711 --> 00:41:55,790
across the hall as if they were half -scared out of their wits.

528
00:41:56,589 --> 00:41:59,010
I am sure she is something not right.

529
00:41:59,889 --> 00:42:01,050
They cried one and all.

530
00:42:01,730 --> 00:42:03,389
She told us such things.

531
00:42:03,955 --> 00:42:05,629
She knows all about us.

532
00:42:06,629 --> 00:42:12,951
And they sank breathless into the various seats the gentleman hastened to bring them.

533
00:42:13,529 --> 00:42:18,730
Pressed for further explanation, they declared she had told them of things

534
00:42:18,730 --> 00:42:21,370
they had said and done when they were mere children.

535
00:42:22,379 --> 00:42:26,470
Described books and ornaments they had in their budwars at home.

536
00:42:27,610 --> 00:42:31,230
Keepsakes that different relations had presented to them.

537
00:42:32,360 --> 00:42:37,269
They affirmed that she had even divined their thoughts, and had whispered in the

538
00:42:37,271 --> 00:42:43,010
ear of each, the name of the person she liked best in the world, and informed them

539
00:42:43,410 --> 00:42:45,330
of what they most wished for.

540
00:42:46,790 --> 00:42:52,010
Hear the gentleman interposed with earnest petitions to be further enlightened on

541
00:42:52,010 --> 00:42:58,790
these two last named points, but they got only blushes, ejaculations, tremors,

542
00:42:59,250 --> 00:43:02,650
and titters, in return for their opportunity.

543
00:43:03,849 --> 00:43:10,330
The matrons mean time offered vinaigrettes and wielded fans, and again and again

544
00:43:10,330 --> 00:43:16,410
reiterated the expression of their concern that their warning had not been taken in

545
00:43:16,411 --> 00:43:20,578
time, and the elder gentleman laughed and the younger

546
00:43:20,580 --> 00:43:24,029
urged their services on the agitated fair ones.

547
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:30,230
In the midst of the tumult, and while my eyes and ears were fully engaged in the

548
00:43:30,230 --> 00:43:34,410
scene before me, I heard a hem close at my elbow.

549
00:43:35,269 --> 00:43:37,449
I turned and saw Sam.

550
00:43:38,760 --> 00:43:43,750
If you please miss, the gypsy declares that there is another young single lady in

551
00:43:43,750 --> 00:43:47,211
the room, who has not been to her yet, and she

552
00:43:47,211 --> 00:43:50,550
swears she will not go till she has seen all.

553
00:43:51,029 --> 00:43:52,230
I thought it must be you.

554
00:43:52,949 --> 00:43:54,330
There is no one else for it.

555
00:43:54,970 --> 00:43:55,989
What shall I tell her?

556
00:43:57,349 --> 00:44:02,730
Oh, I will go by all means, I answered, and I was glad of the unexpected

557
00:44:02,730 --> 00:44:06,550
opportunity to gratify my much-excited curiosity.

558
00:44:07,910 --> 00:44:12,730
I slipped out of the room, unobserved by any eye, for the company were gathered in

559
00:44:12,730 --> 00:44:16,184
one mass about the trembling trio just returned,

560
00:44:16,184 --> 00:44:19,411
and I closed the door quietly behind me.

561
00:44:21,379 --> 00:44:24,936
If you like miss, said Sam, I'll wait in the hall for

562
00:44:24,938 --> 00:44:28,650
you, and if she frightens you, just call and I'll come in.

563
00:44:29,980 --> 00:44:33,769
No, Sam, return to the kitchen, I am not in the least afraid.

564
00:44:35,529 --> 00:44:38,650
Nor was I, but I was a good deal interested and excited.
